{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The portable SSD and microSD card fit my history of external storage and card readers: they offer convenient ways to carry and access files without opening a computer.",
    "The cable organizer feels useful because I have accumulated USB adapters, readers, and cables that I could keep together."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The internal SSDs relate to my storage purchases, but choosing them would require a specific computer upgrade and compatibility checks that I have no current reason to undertake.",
    "The Fire TV Stick Lite duplicates a use already covered by my recent 4K Max bundle, while the iPad case and AirTags assume devices or needs I have not established.",
    "AirPods and Kindle Oasis do not address a current need for me; buying home electronics and Amazon devices does not mean I am looking for earbuds or an ebook reader."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My storage purchases seem to have been treated as interest in any drive, although portable storage and internal upgrades serve different purposes for me.",
    "My use of Amazon devices and Mac-compatible accessories seems to have been stretched into interest in more Amazon and Apple products regardless of their purpose."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent streaming-device purchase matters because it already fills the need another streaming stick would serve.",
    "Accessories feel relevant when they support equipment I have used, such as my card reader, rather than requiring an unconfirmed device.",
    "Many of my purchases solve concrete setup, connection, or replacement needs; a useful addition to that equipment feels more timely than a device with an unrelated purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical electronics accessories but sometimes confused related products with things I currently need."
}"}
